: "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#28364274155", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "University in frankfurt, germany. Goethe University Frankfurt is a public university in Jügelhaus, established in 1914-10-16. Holds notable historical significance, documented across 62 language editions of Wikipedia. Relevant to cause-and-effect analysis.", "newValue": "Goethe University Frankfurt, established on October 16, 1914, in Frankfurt, Germany, represents a pivotal institution in the landscape of modern education and research. Named after the illustrious writer Johann Wolfgang von Goethe, the university has become synonymous with progressive thought and academic excellence in Western Europe. Its founding coincided with a period of significant upheaval and transformation in German society, marked by the lead-up to World War I and the subsequent cultural shifts that defined the 20th century. The university's emphasis on interdisciplinary studies and its commitment to social responsibility reflect broader trends in higher education during this era.

